WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.430
Locate the femoral head on this textbook illustration.

00:00:03.340 --> 00:00:06.850
Chapter forty-five identifies interruption
of its blood supply as

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:09.934
the initiating problem in Legg Calvé Perthes disease.

00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:14.300
The supplied sequence is
necrosis of the ossification center,

00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:17.380
collapse, and gradual remodeling by living bone.

00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:20.546
Watch the highlighted head lose its rounded contour.

00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:24.753
This deformation illustrates the
described collapse; it does not

00:00:24.760 --> 00:00:28.270
reproduce a patient radiograph
or predict the final shape.

00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:32.070
The final stage illustrates
remodeling without promising a complete

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:33.900
return to the original contour.

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:36.990
The packet’s containment goal is to keep the ball

00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:39.913
completely within the
socket, while maintaining motion.

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:42.848
Knee pain can be part of this hip disorder.

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:46.360
The source does not supply a precise recovery timeline

00:00:46.380 --> 00:00:47.507
for this animation.
